Flayr Chop patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

WAV reader: the iXML and axml chunks (free-form XML metadata Flayr Chop never
uses) are no longer parsed, so an audio file never feeds JUCE's XML parser: 2,000
nested elements in a 16 KB WAV's iXML chunk recursed until the 512 KB stack of the
thread loading it ran out (found by an independent review). The XML depth limit
(juce-xml-depth-limit.patch) stops that too; this removes the path altogether.

Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND (cmake/ApplyPatch.cmake).

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_WavAudioFormat.cpp Flayr Chop: no iXML/axml parsing

